summary:
- topic: Board Governance
  text: The Board Chair reported on the development of new board norms and communication
    guidelines over the summer, which were created to improve effectiveness and collaboration.
- topic: Student Report
  text: The student representative provided a comprehensive update on the start of
    the school year, highlighting successful school openings, positive student behavior,
    and new vestibules for safety.
- topic: Nutrition Program
  text: Updates from the nutrition department included the continuation of free meals
    for all students, the appointment of an interim director, and new partnerships
    to provide local fish, culturally relevant greens, and work towards Halal certification.
- topic: Enrollment
  text: The Superintendent reported a district-wide enrollment of 2,771 students,
    a decrease of about 80 students from the previous year, primarily due to a historically
    large graduating class at the high school.
- topic: District Finances
  text: The Superintendent and Finance Committee discussed the FY2025 budget, noting
    recent payroll errors that are being corrected and a planned audit of financial
    processes. There are concerns that the fund balance may have been spent as of
    July 1, 2025, and an external audit is scheduled to begin.
- topic: Budget Development
  text: The administration has begun work on the FY2026-27 budget, with an initial
    focus on controlling spending in operational areas like utilities and overtime.
- topic: Policy
  text: The board discussed Policy JJIF regarding the management of concussions. After
    discussion about ensuring parent/guardian notification and involvement, the board
    voted to send the policy back to the committee for further revision.
- topic: Personnel
  text: The board approved the consent agenda, which included several personnel elections,
    and acknowledged the upcoming retirement of Kim Feline, an instructional support
    staff member at the high school.
